LICENCE PENDING FOUNDER DECISION

The Cloudflare Worker variant of the Puppet Master relay in this folder (`relay/worker`, including
`relay/worker/wasm`) has no licence yet. It follows the same decision as the relay server
(`relay/server`): the founder is choosing between copyleft (AGPL-3.0: open, but a hosted clone must
publish its changes) and proprietary (all rights reserved, closed source, still freely
self-hostable). Until that decision is recorded in `relay/LICENSE`, all rights are reserved and no
licence is granted.

The protocol crate (`relay/protocol`) that the Worker's WebAssembly module is built from is not
covered by this notice: it is MIT-licensed (see `relay/protocol/LICENSE`), so any client can speak to
any relay.
